            <h2 style="page-break-before:always" class="qz-heading qz-heading-level-1">
                <span class="qz-heading-number">5</span>Project Training
            </h2>
            <h3 style="" class="qz-heading qz-heading-level-2">
                <span class="qz-heading-number">5.1</span>Training Summary
            </h3>
            <p style="text-align:justify">
                <span t-field="doc.company_id.name"/>
                will be delivering online training including trainers of the frontline employees and admin/system
                administrator<span t-field="doc.partner_id.name"/>.
            </p>
            <p style="text-align:justify">Training will be delivered in English.</p>
            <p style="text-align:justify">The Training Plan identifies the key elements and steps necessary for training
                the staff on the use of the components of the system proposed by
                <span t-field="doc.company_id.name"/>
                to highlight the main functionalities and benefits.
            </p>
            <p style="text-align:justify">After the final deployment of the application,
                <span t-field="doc.company_id.name"/>
                conducts a thorough training covering all the modules of the solution ensuring that the solution is
                fully grasped by all users prior to going live.
            </p>
            <h3 style="" class="qz-heading qz-heading-level-2">
                <span class="qz-heading-number">5.2</span>Training Objectives
            </h3>
            <p style="text-align:justify">The training courses allow the users to discover the solution, operate, and
                manage its various functions. The training covers the utilization as well as parameterization and
                administration of the application to optimize and streamline the operations. The main objectives are:
            </p>
            <ul class="qz-bullets">
                <li>Enable users and administrator
                    <span t-field="doc.partner_id.name"/>
                    to gain an overall understanding of the scope and purpose of the overall solution.
                </li>
                <li>Provide each user with hands-on experience around the system’s functions.</li>
                <li>Share knowledge and functional use of the solution while ensuring that
                    <span t-field="doc.partner_id.name"/>
                    has the total ownership to carry out all duties and operations by themselves.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <h3 style="" class="qz-heading qz-heading-level-2">
                <span class="qz-heading-number">5.3</span>Roles &amp; Responsibilities
            </h3>
            <p style="">Admin (system administrator<span t-field="doc.partner_id.name"/>) is responsible for keeping the
                systems operational, keeping the content up-to-date and safe by performing regular backups.
            </p>
            <p style="text-align:justify">Trainers of the frontline users are responsible for training the remaining
                employees of the team.
            </p>
            <h2 style="page-break-before:always" class="qz-heading qz-heading-level-1">
                <span class="qz-heading-number">6</span>Post Implementation Services
            </h2>
            <h3 style="" class="qz-heading qz-heading-level-2">
                <span class="qz-heading-number">6.1</span>Support &amp; Maintenance Services Plan
            </h3>
            <p style="text-align:justify">
                <span t-field="doc.company_id.name"/>
                provides warranty services for one (1) month upon project go-live and after-sales maintenance services
                for one (1) year upon the warranty expiration, through an Annual Maintenance Contract.
            </p>
            <p style="text-align:justify">
                <span t-field="doc.company_id.name"/>
                will be responsible in maintaining all system functionalities and ensure that integrations are up and
                running.
                <span t-field="doc.company_id.name"/>
                customer support services cover phone, portal, e-mail and online support. On-Site support is not
                required.
            </p>
            <p style="">The below SLA is applicable to all tickets that are initiated during the support period.</p>
            <p style="">The services cover the following issues:</p>
            <ul class="qz-bullets">
                <li>Core solution Bugs.</li>
                <li>Issues with operating the application as per the agreed functional specifications document signed
                    and agreed between both parties.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p style="text-align:justify">Version Upgrades are not covered into the support and maintenance services.
                For any version upgrade, a change request should be agreed on between
                <span t-field="doc.company_id.name"/>
                and
                <span t-field="doc.partner_id.name"/>
                and will be quoted separately.
            </p>
            <p style="">
                <span t-field="doc.company_id.name"/>
                will reserve the right to not to provide any Maintenance and Support cases where it appears that:
            </p>
            <ul class="qz-bullets">
                <li>In the event the payment or services is past due,
                    <span t-field="doc.company_id.name"/>
                    at its discretion may suspend the rights of the licensee to receive the services for which payment
                    is past due until full payment is made.
                </li>
                <li>The Solution is amended/changed by non-authorized party without prior notice to
                    <span t-field="doc.company_id.name"/>
                    support contact person.
                </li>
                <li>An error of the Solution has occurred because of the user’s negligent conduct or incorrect use of
                    the solution.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <h3 style="page-break-before:always" class="qz-heading qz-heading-level-2">
                <span class="qz-heading-number">6.2</span>Response Mechanism
            </h3>
            <p style="">
                <span t-field="doc.company_id.name"/>
                incident response time is divided according to the following criteria:
            </p>
            <ul class="qz-bullets">
                <li>
                    <strong>Level 1 severity: Serious Incidents;</strong>
                    these incidents happen due to a system crash. They are of highest priority, thus having a response
                    time of four (4) working hours. The objective is to have a workaround within the eight (8) working
                    hour’s timeframe else if it is impossible will be escalated within
                    <span t-field="doc.company_id.name"/>
                    and
                    <span t-field="doc.partner_id.name"/>
                    with the appropriate action plan.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Level 2 severity: Average Incidents;</strong>
                    these incidents are not as serious, thus having less priority. They can be system configuration
                    problem. The response time is eight (8) working hours. The objective is to have a workaround within
                    the twenty-four (24) working hour’s timeframe.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Level 3 severity: Minor Incidents and Improvements;</strong>
                    these incidents include adding new functionalities to the system. These are minor changes, hence not
                    being urgent. The response time is two (2) working days and implementation action plan is provided
                    to the client’s approval.
                </li>
            </ul>
